{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790981856,"nonce":"uMsYxMU9EGg9KPRZ2/ZkzCgcr4A=","title":"Making a signal while a computed evaluates deadlocks","message":"Signal.make called inside a Computed's function (for example a lazily created signal read for the first time inside a computed) hangs: the computed runs inside Blinc's reactive-graph lock (computed_from -\u003e create_derived), and blinc_signal_* -\u003e new_state -\u003e signal() takes the same non-reentrant mutex. Seen as smoke hanging in ashui.theme.Theme before its signals were made eagerly (sample: get_derived -\u003e computed_from -\u003e call_void -\u003e ... -\u003e blinc_signal_i32 -\u003e ReactiveGraph lock).\n\nSolidJS allows creating signals inside a computation. ashui should either support it (on the Haxe side: queue the creation until the evaluation returns, or make the signal lazily on first set/get outside the lock) or fail loudly instead of hanging (Guard can tell it is inside an evaluation). Theme works around it with Theme.ready().","files":null}]}